# ##planr-devops-agent:begin## (managed block — SPEC-013; preserve hand-edits outside this block)
#
# .env.example — planr-pipeline
#
# planr-pipeline is a Claude Code plugin distributed as markdown + stdlib JS.
# It has NO runtime server, NO database, and NO long-lived process.
# There are therefore NO application environment variables to configure.
#
# The only environment interaction at runtime is:
#   - Node >=20 on PATH (see package.json "engines")
#   - The Claude Code host injects plugin context automatically
#
# If you add an env var to the plugin in the future, document it here with
# a placeholder value (never a real secret), e.g.:
#
#   PLANR_LOG_LEVEL=info
#   PLANR_MAX_PARALLEL=4
#
# ##planr-devops-agent:end##
